WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.111
A bonus lap for the builders.

2
00:00:03.111 --> 00:00:08.054
Everything the series showed has an
API underneath — this episode walks the

3
00:00:08.054 --> 00:00:11.283
developer surface: keys,
webhooks, coding agents,

4
00:00:11.283 --> 00:00:13.590
and the sandbox that contains them.

5
00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.729
Programmatic access
starts here: named keys,

6
00:00:17.729 --> 00:00:21.002
one per system — the
ingest pipeline, the CI job.

7
00:00:21.002 --> 00:00:26.412
Each is scoped, revocable in one click,
and every call it makes lands in the same

8
00:00:26.412 --> 00:00:28.550
audit log you saw in the finale.

9
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:34.218
Four doors for four styles: a
REST API for everything the UI does,

10
00:00:34.218 --> 00:00:37.061
MCP to serve Tale’s tools to other agents,

11
00:00:37.061 --> 00:00:40.107
WebDAV to mount
workspace files like a drive,

12
00:00:40.107 --> 00:00:43.628
and sandbox runtimes you
can configure per language.

13
00:00:44.828 --> 00:00:48.532
Webhooks point the other way:
any system can fire an agent.

14
00:00:48.532 --> 00:00:51.357
A signed POST from your
CRM, your monitoring,

15
00:00:51.357 --> 00:00:55.124
your build — and the agent
runs with the payload as context.

16
00:00:55.124 --> 00:00:58.828
The automations from episode
five, triggered from anywhere.

17
00:01:00.028 --> 00:01:04.250
And the heavy machinery:
external coding agents — Claude Code,

18
00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:08.745
Cursor, and their peers — work
inside Tale in their own sandboxes.

19
00:01:08.745 --> 00:01:14.057
They plan, write files, run commands…
inside a box that starts empty and stays

20
00:01:14.057 --> 00:01:17.258
disconnected except for
what the policy allows.

21
00:01:18.458 --> 00:01:22.730
That policy is explicit and
yours: which packages may install,

22
00:01:22.730 --> 00:01:24.591
which hosts code may reach.

23
00:01:24.591 --> 00:01:28.243
Cloud metadata and private
ranges are always refused,

24
00:01:28.243 --> 00:01:33.618
and when the egress proxy is down,
nothing gets out — the system fails closed,

25
00:01:33.618 --> 00:01:34.376
never open.

26
00:01:35.576 --> 00:01:41.084
Power tools, contained blast radius —
the developer version of everything this

27
00:01:41.084 --> 00:01:42.073
series taught.

28
00:01:42.073 --> 00:01:45.674
Scope the key, sign the
webhook, sandbox the agent,

29
00:01:45.674 --> 00:01:48.216
and build boldly inside those lines.

30
00:01:49.416 --> 00:01:52.004
That was the series — all ten episodes.

31
00:01:52.004 --> 00:01:56.118
The develop section of the
documentation takes over from here:

32
00:01:56.118 --> 00:02:00.165
API reference, webhook
signatures, and the contributor guide.

33
00:02:00.165 --> 00:02:01.558
Build something good.

34
00:02:02.758 --> 00:02:04.808
Thanks for building with Tale.

